.TH geectl-build-job-history 1  "geectl-build-job-history 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-job\-history \- List the build jobs that ran in a repository, newest first
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build job\-history\fR [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-code\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIREPOSITORY\fR> <\fIARCH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the build jobs that ran in a repository, newest first
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
Only jobs for this package
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
At most this many entries
.TP
\fB\-\-code\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Only jobs with this result code (e.g. `failed`)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the repository is in
.TP
<\fIREPOSITORY\fR>
The repository the jobs ran in
.TP
<\fIARCH\fR>
The architecture the jobs ran on
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
